{{thought {version #1}}
 {title There Is No Such Thing as a Leftist Twitch Streamer}
 {published #"2026/09/26 12:51 +0100"}
 {uuid 61959614-b730-4036-af65-28e57f2e8afe}
 {description
  Twitch streamers are capitalists.
  They sell entertainment occasionally with a political veneer, and their objective is to maximise their viewership and thus profits for Amazon, the provider of the Twitch service.
  A successful advocate of leftism will make people get out of their house and take action within their community.
  This is in direct opposition to the goal of a successful streamer, which is to keep people in their house and watching the stream for as long as possible.
  The algorithmic natural selection pressure in Twitch (and many other platforms) will mean that the most successful {q leftist} creators are those who are the least successful at leftist advocacy.
  A creator with better advocacy would naturally have lower viewership, be recommended less, and so lose to one who is a better streamer and worse political advocate.
  It would do you well to remember that almost all social media is capitalist.
  The content shown to you is selected primarily based on the metric of what makes the most money for capitalists, rather than any altruistic aim.}}
